  "body": "### Summary\nFollow-up of LOT-118 (#209, PR #640, merged as d1c7b74): small fixes from the Opus review (https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/pull/640#issuecomment-6735079981). They did not block the merge, and fixing them in #640 would have cost another macOS CI run. **M4.**\n\n### Scope\n1. **Low.** `App/SwiftHFR/Settings/PseudoListEditorView.swift:42`, `PseudoListEditorModel.swift:87`. A swipe-delete turns row offsets into pseudos inside its background task. Two quick deletes can remove the wrong member, and a deleted row can flash back.\n   - Fix: resolve the pseudos at swipe time, drop them from the list at once, then write.\n   - Test: two quick deletes remove the two swiped members.\n2. **Low.** `App/SwiftHFR/Reader/TopicReaderView.swift:303`. The profile hook passed when a link opens a profile holds the reader model strongly, against the \"weak captures only\" rule (`UserProfileModel.swift:71`).\n   - Fix: build a `[weak model]` closure once in `makeController`.\n3. **Nit.** `App/SwiftHFR/Settings/PseudoListManager.swift:15-21`. The footers cite legacy `:571-578` but are reworded.\n   - Fix: restore the legacy wording, or name the difference in the comment.\n4. **Nit.** `docs/lots/LOT-118-blacklist-whitelist.md:37`. The \"Avatar menu (#595)\" paragraph is out of date since #638 merged.\n5. **Nit.** The profile's list buttons do not announce the toggle to VoiceOver, unlike the same action in the message menu.\n\n### Mac check (on #640)\nOn iPad, a reader left visible beside Plus › Réglages picks up an edit made in the Blacklist / Whitelist editors.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- One PR, iterated as a draft.\n- Swift Testing tests for item 1.\n- Opus review.\n- Rule #620 ledger only if an entry changes.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
